# Fork-authored (CUSTOM-20260923-001). Upstream has no .gitattributes, and this machine has
# core.autocrlf=true (system AND user level). Without this file a fresh clone checks out *.sh
# as CRLF and `sh script.sh` misbehaves, and every build-regenerated file shows a phantom
# "modified" status. Upstream blobs are already LF in the index, so adding this introduces no
# renormalization noise.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.wasm binary
*.vsix binary

# Windows-native script formats: cmd.exe and Windows PowerShell expect CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
